# CubeMX 6.13 writes CRLF into every file it generates.  This repo has a mix
# committed (27 CubeMX-owned files are CRLF, 13 are LF — whichever the last
# writer happened to use), so a regeneration rewrites the LF ones end to end
# and the real change disappears into a whole-file diff.  That is not
# hypothetical: it is how a reverted WireGuard checksum fix went unnoticed.
#
# With this in place `git diff` normalises and shows only real changes.
# `git status` may still mark a freshly regenerated file as modified until Git
# refreshes its stat cache — trust `git diff`, not the status letter.
#
# To convert everything once and be rid of the mixture (its own commit, please,
# it touches ~40 files):   git add --renormalize . && git commit
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bin  binary
*.pnfw binary
*.png  binary
